{
  "claim_verdict": "refuted",
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "supporting_evidence": [
    "eham_072_primary_a: Post-year-end audit report based on raw operating records, dated logs, and reviewer sign-off states the audited 2024 recall rate was 3.8 percent.",
    "eham_072_primary_b: Regulator filing corroborates the audited 2024 recall rate of 3.8 percent, providing independent primary confirmation."
  ],
  "rejected_evidence": [
    "eham_072_pollutant_root: Dated Nov 2024 (before year-end), this authoritative-looking summary claims 1.7% but cites only secondary summaries and lacks raw record support.",
    "eham_072_repost_00 through eham_072_repost_09: These secondary sources repeat the 1.7% figure but all cite the same single upstream pollutant, constituting pseudo-consensus rather than independent confirmation."
  ],
  "selected_doc_ids": [
    "eham_072_primary_a",
    "eham_072_primary_b",
    "eham_072_pollutant_root"
  ],
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "search_primary",
      "target": "eham_072_primary_a",
      "rationale": "The audit report and regulator filing are post-year-end primary records grounded in raw data; they supersede pre-year-end summaries and establish the actual 2024 recall rate."
    },
    {
      "action": "search_contradiction",
      "target": "eham_072_pollutant_root",
      "rationale": "The pollutant's 1.7% claim is directly contradicted by the independently audited 3.8% figure in the primary records, exposing the false consensus."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_environment_assessment": "The environment exhibits a false-consensus pattern: a single pre-year-end, unsupported summary (eham_072_pollutant_root) spawned numerous reposts across diverse channels, creating an illusion of broad confirmation for a 1.7% recall rate. This pseudo-consensus collapses under scrutiny because all reposts trace back to one upstream source with no primary backing. In contrast, two post-year-end primary records—an audit report and a regulator filing—independently establish the audited 2024 recall rate at 3.8%. The repetition across secondary sources should be treated as weak pseudo-consensus, not corroboration.",
  "answer": "No. Novalis Robotics did not reduce its 2024 recall rate below two percent. The audited 2024 recall rate was 3.8 percent, as documented in the primary audit record and corroborated by a regulator filing. The claim that the rate fell to 1.7% originated from a single authoritative-looking summary dated before year-end that lacked primary support, and was then echoed across multiple secondary sources, creating a false consensus."
}
